    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 110\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 916, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the judiciary law, in relation to requiring town\n      and village courts compensate temporary interpreters for  deaf  or\n      hard of hearing persons\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill would increase the reimbursement counties must provide town\nand village courts for temporary court interpreter fees from $25 per day\nto $110, shifting the cost of providing services from one unit of  local\ngovernment  to  the  other.  Issues  regarding  cost sharing among local\ngovernments should be addressed in the State Budget process where aid to\nlocalities can be considered. Therefore, I am constrained to  veto  this\nlegislation.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
